      "body": "<!-- Thank you for your contribution! Please follow these guidelines to enhance your pull request. If anything is unclear, submit your PR and reach out to maintainers for assistance. Join our Slack community at https://slack.sglang.io to discuss further. -->\n\n## Motivation\nThe meta-models/Muse-Glimmer-30B model can be configured with TP=6 and launched successfully in a CPU environment.\n\nThe following three dimensions are not divisible by 6:\n- Number of visual attention heads: 16\n- Visual MLP intermediate dimension: 8960\n- Vision adapter intermediate layer: 4096\n\n## Modifications\n\nZero-padding logic applied:\n1. Visual heads padded from 16 to 18; visual MLP intermediate dimension padded from 8960 to 9024.\n2. `VisionAttention `and visual RoPE switched to use `config.head_dim`; `projection_size` updated to `heads * head_dim` (18 × 96 = 1728).\n3. To satisfy AMX GEMM alignment requirements for input dimensions per shard (IC % 32), the adapter's fc1 output/fc2 input dimension is rounded up to the nearest multiple of `tp * 32` (4096 → 4224).\n\n## Accuracy Tests\nThe model starts up correctly, and the accuracy of responses for both text and image inputs is normal.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38201402476](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38201402476)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38201402197](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38201402197)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38201402380](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38201402380)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
